analysisWe need to read the Java code and produce an assert statement matching the comment starting with "@@@". The comment is in pollLast method: 

```java
public E pollLast() {
    final Node<E> l = last;
    return (l == null) ? null : unlinkLast(l);
    // @@@ If the list is initially empty, then the result is null.
}
```

We need to express specification: "If the list is initially empty, then the result is null."

We need to refer to the initial state of the list before method execution. The predicate "list is initially empty" means before the method call, size == 0 or isEmpty() true. Use \old(this.isEmpty()) or \old(this.size()) == 0. Use observer methods: there is size() and isEmpty(). Use this.isEmpty() maybe. Use \old(this.isEmpty()).

Result is \result.

Thus assert: \old(this.isEmpty()) => \result == null

But need to ensure correct syntax: \old(this.isEmpty()) => \result == null

Maybe need parentheses: (\old(this.isEmpty())) => (\result == null)

But they said lower priority, so parentheses recommended.

Thus final answer:

<code>assert \old(this.isEmpty()) => \result == null;</code>

Check if need to refer to size: \old(this.size()) == 0 => \result == null

Either is fine. Use isEmpty.

Thus final.assistantfinal<code>assert \old(this.isEmpty()) => \result == null;</code>
